Explanation:
Functions used: df.nunique(), df.nlargest()
Usage: df.nunique() to find unique elements in dataframe, df.nlargest() to find largest elements in dataframe
Interpretation: If the platform recommends songs based only on stream counts, users may be shown tracks that many listeners abandon quickly.
A better recommendation system should balance streams with skip rates, completion rates, and user feedback.
